{"title":"2002 IMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Problems of the 2002 <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO\">IMO</a>.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_I\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day I</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_II\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day II</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_I\">Day I</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day I\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is the set of all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/9/169720b6d97c7c69f8f8a740ff74dee5dbc96419.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(h,k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/5/355a14a751eaaf940322e7c9f0b6843d94d8a7c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h,k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" /> non-negative integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/6/0f640cc484c10ec3b90fadcce22464decd8cf4e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h + k &lt; n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"77\" height=\"14\" />. Each element of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is colored red or blue, so that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/9/169720b6d97c7c69f8f8a740ff74dee5dbc96419.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(h,k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"18\" /> is red and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/8/3087b5bac0cb854263ab33b0148066fe58cff26a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h&#39; \\le h,k&#39; \\le k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"19\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/a/59a8714ad90a8bc86c57788d6eb25e92f6a8bda7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(h&#39;,k&#39;)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" /> is also red. A type <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> subset of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> blue elements with different first member and a type <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> subset of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> blue elements with different second member. Show that there are the same number of type <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and type <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> subsets.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2002 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is a diameter of a circle center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is any point on the circle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/c/a6cd34a211696ff9f8dbf820fb384c0acd73967b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AOC \\not\\le 60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"18\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is the chord which is the perpendicular bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c53cc93aa43cc55bea0dc2511833fe6bdda020f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of the minor arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. The line through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> meets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb5588023cfa1ac14643e9778699f03eecc57a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />. Show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb5588023cfa1ac14643e9778699f03eecc57a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is the incenter of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/c/a9c5f98c6f70b855ea3d874c757247f6dfbbac5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CEF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2002 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Find all pairs of positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/a/a2a2adab76f687304804389ccc3ccd277c781fbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m,n \\ge 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"17\" /> for which here exist infinitely many positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> such that \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/f/a2f11c66fd6ec13bf2fbae5a495ce00aed16537f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a^m+a-1}{a^n+a^2-1}\\]\" width=\"89\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>is itself an integer.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2002 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_II\">Day II</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day II\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/65262bf247c4a3c6114a8223d249dc9702619d3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> be an integer and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/a/32a29db56a2450439fc073f630d275c66e51a169.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1=d_{1}&lt;d_{2}&lt;d_{3} \\cdots &lt;d_{r}=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"235\" height=\"17\" /> be all of its positive divisors in increasing order. Show that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/8/608616f515bb5ffcfb1c6b277b9e3867bbdc27fa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d=d_1d_2+d_2d_3+ \\cdots +d_{r-1}d_r &lt;n^2.\\]\" width=\"285\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2002 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Find all functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/1/b61db202acc1a61dfd78c59903be29913fc09cdd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f:\\Bbb{R}\\to \\Bbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"18\" /> such that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/2/c92c29ce2db1e17848b4da5f6f018c0f03021faa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(f(x)+f(z))(f(y)+f(t))=f(xy-zt)+f(xt+yz)\\]\" width=\"418\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>for all real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/e/8ceeecfb3f2d34c661d402c5c7c0285427f70b00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z,t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2002 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/1/8f1e2533d6abdb11a9a1626c0240fab1a9200fc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> be a positive integer.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/3/293a1b7c57186fcb055c7c2e44308a0b187e1227.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_1,C_2,...,C_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"104\" height=\"18\" /> be unit circles in the plane, with centers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/5/ef5dd65e58eda5e903491856b737d1a249779acc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1,O_2,...,O_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"18\" /> respectively.  If no line meets more than two of the circles, prove that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/e/02e757c70af2e01d6d7185ec783c533594060872.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{1\\le i&lt; j \\le n}^{}\\frac{1}{O_iO_j}\\le\\frac{(n-1)\\pi}{4}\\]\" width=\"197\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2002 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO\" title=\"2002 IMO\">2002 IMO</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions,_with_authors\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors\">IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competition_resources\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competition resources\">Mathematics competition resources</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO\" title=\"2002 IMO\">2002 IMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO\" title=\"2001 IMO\">2001 IMO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2002 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2002 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2002 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2002 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2002 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2002 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_IMO\" title=\"2003 IMO\">2003 IMO</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017152441\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.031 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.047 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 270/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 836/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 56/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7635/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.198      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    7.198      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:28042:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017152441 and revision id 221709. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}